{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FocusManager"},{"type":"text","value":" manages the focus state within React Query."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It can be used to change the default event listeners or to manually change the focus state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Its available methods are:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#focusmanagerseteventlistener","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setEventListener"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#focusmanagersetfocused","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setFocused"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#focusmanagerisfocused","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isFocused"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"focusmanager-seteventlistener","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusManager.setEventListener"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setEventListener"},{"type":"text","value":" can be used to set a custom event listener:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { focusManager } from 'react-query'\n\nfocusManager.setEventListener(handleFocus => {\n  // Listen to visibilitychange and focus\n  if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.addEventListener) {\n    window.addEventListener('visibilitychange', handleFocus, false)\n    window.addEventListener('focus', handleFocus, false)\n  }\n\n  return () => {\n    // Be sure to unsubscribe if a new handler is set\n    window.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', handleFocus)\n    window.removeEventListener('focus', handleFocus)\n  }\n})","lang":"js"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"focusmanager-setfocused","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusManager.setFocused"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setFocused"},{"type":"text","value":" can be used to manually set the focus state. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" to fallback to the default focus check."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { focusManager } from 'react-query'\n\n// Set focused\nfocusManager.setFocused(true)\n\n// Set unfocused\nfocusManager.setFocused(false)\n\n// Fallback to the default focus check\nfocusManager.setFocused(undefined)","lang":"js"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focused: boolean | undefined"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"focusmanager-isfocused","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusManager.isFocused"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isFocused"},{"type":"text","value":" can be used to get the current focus state."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const isFocused = focusManager.isFocused()","lang":"js"}],"headings":[{"id":"focusmanager-seteventlistener","text":"focusManager.setEventListener","level":2},{"id":"focusmanager-setfocused","text":"focusManager.setFocused","level":2},{"id":"focusmanager-isfocused","text":"focusManager.isFocused","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `FocusManager` manages the focus state within React Query.\n\nIt can be used to change the default event listeners or to manually change the focus state.\n\nIts available methods are:\n\n- [`setEventListener`](#focusmanagerseteventlistener)\n- [`setFocused`](#focusmanagersetfocused)\n- [`isFocused`](#focusmanagerisfocused)\n\n## `focusManager.setEventListener`\n\n`setEventListener` can be used to set a custom event listener:\n\n```js\nimport { focusManager } from 'react-query'\n\nfocusManager.setEventListener(handleFocus => {\n  // Listen to visibilitychange and focus\n  if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.addEventListener) {\n    window.addEventListener('visibilitychange', handleFocus, false)\n    window.addEventListener('focus', handleFocus, false)\n  }\n\n  return () => {\n    // Be sure to unsubscribe if a new handler is set\n    window.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', handleFocus)\n    window.removeEventListener('focus', handleFocus)\n  }\n})\n```\n\n## `focusManager.setFocused`\n\n`setFocused` can be used to manually set the focus state. Set `undefined` to fallback to the default focus check.\n\n```js\nimport { focusManager } from 'react-query'\n\n// Set focused\nfocusManager.setFocused(true)\n\n// Set unfocused\nfocusManager.setFocused(false)\n\n// Fallback to the default focus check\nfocusManager.setFocused(undefined)\n```\n\n**Options**\n\n- `focused: boolean | undefined`\n\n## `focusManager.isFocused`\n\n`isFocused` can be used to get the current focus state.\n\n```js\nconst isFocused = focusManager.isFocused()\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: FocusManager\ntitle: FocusManager\n---\n\nThe `FocusManager` manages the focus state within React Query.\n\nIt can be used to change the default event listeners or to manually change the focus state.\n\nIts available methods are:\n\n- [`setEventListener`](#focusmanagerseteventlistener)\n- [`setFocused`](#focusmanagersetfocused)\n- [`isFocused`](#focusmanagerisfocused)\n\n## `focusManager.setEventListener`\n\n`setEventListener` can be used to set a custom event listener:\n\n```js\nimport { focusManager } from 'react-query'\n\nfocusManager.setEventListener(handleFocus => {\n  // Listen to visibilitychange and focus\n  if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.addEventListener) {\n    window.addEventListener('visibilitychange', handleFocus, false)\n    window.addEventListener('focus', handleFocus, false)\n  }\n\n  return () => {\n    // Be sure to unsubscribe if a new handler is set\n    window.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', handleFocus)\n    window.removeEventListener('focus', handleFocus)\n  }\n})\n```\n\n## `focusManager.setFocused`\n\n`setFocused` can be used to manually set the focus state. Set `undefined` to fallback to the default focus check.\n\n```js\nimport { focusManager } from 'react-query'\n\n// Set focused\nfocusManager.setFocused(true)\n\n// Set unfocused\nfocusManager.setFocused(false)\n\n// Fallback to the default focus check\nfocusManager.setFocused(undefined)\n```\n\n**Options**\n\n- `focused: boolean | undefined`\n\n## `focusManager.isFocused`\n\n`isFocused` can be used to get the current focus state.\n\n```js\nconst isFocused = focusManager.isFocused()\n```\n"}
